Z||000000||Simple Fiero||07-21-2001||07:13 PM||||I am having a bit of a problem and have heard some many different things, like you don't know how to drive a 5 speed or give it time, or it didn't jerk when I drove it. When ever I disengage the gas pedal at speed the car jerks, whenever I shift it jerks, it grinds sometimes into reverse, and first and sometimes not. Now I have driven standards before and never have they jerked like this car. If I don't figure this out I am going to have to get rid of it, my significant other can't take it (bad back). I don't want to but you do what you have to for love. Any help would be great. Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mach10||07-21-2001||08:55 PM||||Engine mounts. ORRrrrr, you can't drive a 5-spd   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>My SchMazda had a similar problem. Go easier on the clutch, or else change the mounts. You shouldn't have to pull the engine, although it'll probably be a PITA. At least the parts are cheap... Sorry   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>LOL, I just realized I'll be driving thru Kelowna in 5 days  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I'll take a look for you then  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 07-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||07-21-2001||11:23 PM||||Start with taking a good look at your "dog bone" torque mount (is the rubber come away from the aluminum).  If this is worn out it will cause this problem.  And as mentioned above maybe all your mtr mounts have worn out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||07-22-2001||10:35 AM||||Any oil leaks in that area that is evident?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Simple Fiero||07-22-2001||08:09 PM||||No there isn't an oil lead on that car, and I did my painting today and now my car looks so good especially since I took that crappy pin striping off(it was self done, not by me)<BR>I will replace the dog bonme when i can afford to, thanks for the suggestions.||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||07-22-2001||08:33 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A>  get thier dogbone.<P>You're not going to like this of $69 is a streatch, but it MAY be your clutch has broken a spring or two...  and needs replacement.<P>My car is jerkey now too, and I suspect than when it hit the curb, a spring broke. Because that's all that's left that hasn't been replaced. Uuunnngh.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000006||ROB MAC||07-23-2001||02:33 PM||||My car did the same and got worse as the O2 sensor was failing. Replacement fixed all.||||reg||1
Z||000007||StuGood||07-23-2001||03:54 PM||||When you say it sometimes grinds into 1st and reverse, and it jerks when you shift gears, it suggests to me that the clutch isn't always releasing fully.   Might want to inspect the linkage from front to back, to see if something is hanging up.  ||||reg||1
